*******************************************************************************
                      What Is New in PCBoard 15.41
                      pcbirc crew — August 2026
*******************************************************************************

PCBoard Additions/Changes
=========================

CNAMES.ADD Extension — FilebaseFlags
-------------------------------------
The 64-byte Reserved field in each CNAMES.ADD conference record has been
redefined as FilebaseFlags[64]. This provides per-filebase bit flags with
one bit per filebase, supporting up to 512 filebases per conference.

  Bit 0: FBFLAG_ISO — marks a filebase as ISO/CD-ROM backed
  Bits 1-7: Reserved for future use

PCBoard 15.4 zero-initializes these bytes and never reads them. PCBSM
skips them during conference operations (via ADDCONFRESERVE). All existing
15.4 installations are forward-compatible — no upgrade utility needed.

See docs/devkit/CNAMES.DOC for the original field documentation.
See PCBSRC/LIB/H/NEWDATA.H for the FilebaseFlags definition.


New Utility — PCBISO (ISO/CD-ROM File Area Indexer)
---------------------------------------------------
PCBISO is a standalone utility for managing ISO/CD-ROM file areas.
It reads CNAMES.@@@ and CNAMES.ADD to find configured file areas,
scans source paths, and generates PCBoard DIR listing text files
with automatic FILE_ID.DIZ extraction from ZIP archives.

Commands:
  PCBISO /INDEX <path> <dirfile>      Scan path, generate DIR listing
  PCBISO /INDEX ALL <cnames> <add>    Index all ISO-backed conferences
  PCBISO /REBUILD <path> <dirfile>    Delete and regenerate DIR listing
  PCBISO /LIST <cnames> <add>         List configured file areas
  PCBISO /STATUS <cnames> <add>       Detailed status with file counts
  PCBISO /SETISO <conf> <fb> <add>    Mark filebase as ISO-backed
  PCBISO /CLEARISO <conf> <fb> <add>  Clear ISO flag
  PCBISO /MOUNT <iso>                 Register ISO in mount table
  PCBISO /UNMOUNT <drive>             Release drive letter

Location: PCBSRC/MAIN/SOURCE/UTIL/PCBISO/
Works on PCBoard 15.4+ — no upgrade needed.


New Utility Suite — QFront (FidoNet Mailer)
-------------------------------------------
Clean-room FidoNet mailer suite. 9,112 lines, 20 source files, GPLv3.
5 programs: qfront (orchestrator), qscan (tosser/scanner), qnlist
(nodelist compiler), qfconfig (TUI config editor), qfutil (utility).

Protocols: EMSI/WaZOO, Zmodem, Xmodem, SEAlink
Standards: FTS-5005 BSO, FTS-5001 nodelist, FTS-0001 PKT, FSC-0056 EMSI

Location: tools/qfront/
See tools/qfront/INSTALL.TXT for PCBoard 15.3/15.4 setup instructions.


PCBTEXT String Additions
------------------------
The four PCBTEXT strings added in 15.4 (slots 747-750) are documented
in PCB154.NEW. No additional PCBTEXT strings were added in 15.41.


PCBOARD.DAT
-----------
No changes to PCBOARD.DAT in 15.41. The file format remains at 349 lines
(same as 15.3). Future extensions will append lines after 349 following
Clark's established pattern — see docs/devkit/PCBDAT.DOC.


Compiler Change
---------------
PCBoard 15.41 is compiled with OpenWatcom 2.0 (openwatcom2irc fork)
replacing Borland C++ 3.1. All 28 Clark binaries target DOS4G.
Borland-specific code (inline ASM, conio.h, dos.h) replaced with
Watcom-compatible equivalents.


Bug Fixes
---------
26 bugs fixed across pcbis (11), pcbfoss (6), and QFront (9).
See docs/PCB1541-PHASES.md for the complete bug list.


Developer Documentation
-----------------------
Clark's original developer kit (Develop.zip) has been extracted to
docs/devkit/ with all 23 file format specification documents including:

  PCBDAT.DOC   — PCBOARD.DAT file format (text, one field per line)
  CNAMES.DOC   — CNAMES.@@@ and CNAMES.ADD conference file formats
  USERS.DOC    — Users file format
  MSGS.DOC     — Message base format
  DIR.DOC      — DIR listing format
  STRUCTS.DOC  — General data structures

Full list: docs/devkit/README.1ST
